ModelHub — attribution for third-party data
===========================================

The source code in this repository is MIT licensed. The datasets under /data are derived
from the third-party sources below and remain subject to their licences. Attribution is a
condition of all of them.

CHANGES MADE TO THE ORIGINAL DATA
  The data in /data is modified. ModelHub does not redistribute these sources verbatim.
  For every source listed below, ModelHub:
    - normalises model names into a single canonical registry, merging vendor variants
      (effort levels, thinking modes, date stamps) that the sources publish separately;
    - rescales values onto a common 0-100 axis, including a min-max normalisation of
      LMArena's Bradley-Terry ratings across the cohort present in each build;
    - aggregates per-task scores into category averages (LiveBench);
    - combines figures from several independent sources into a weighted composite score
      that exists nowhere in the original data and is ModelHub's own calculation;
    - filters and rejects source snapshots that fail internal quality checks.
  The originals remain available at the URLs below. Where the two disagree, the original
  source is authoritative and ModelHub's derived figure is not.

